      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">The enzyme transfers a segment of a (1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;alpha;-D-glucan to a new position in an acceptor, which may be glucose or a (1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;alpha;-D-glucan. This entry covers the former separate entry for EC 2.4.1.3 (amylomaltase). The plant enzyme has been termed D-enzyme. An enzymic activity of this nature forms part of the mammalian and yeast glycogen debranching system (see |FRAME: 3.2.1.33-RXN &quot;EC 3.2.1.33, amylo-&amp;alpha;-1,6-glucosidase&quot;|).</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="RXN-1828" />
      <Property key="EC_Number" value="EC-2.4.1.25" />
      <Property key="ReactionEquation" value="Long-linear-glucans + ALPHA-GLUCOSE &lt;=&gt; Short-Alpha-14-Glucans" />
      <Property key="ReactionDirection" value="REVERSIBLE" />
      <Property key="BalanceStatus" value=":UNBALANCED-UNFIXABLE" />
